<summary>
1. Primary Request and Intent:

The user requested a complete spec-to-implementation pipeline for the Praxia Plugin Interface:
1. Oracle critique/revise cycle on the spec at `~/.praxia/docs/specs/260526_praxia-plugin-interface.md` until APPROVE verdict, surfacing design questions as needed
2. Planner+plan-auditor critique/revise cycle until PASS verdict
3. Present the approved implementation plan
4. Fan out fixer agents to execute all phases

After plan approval, the user said "proceed" — triggering full parallel implementation execution.

---

2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **Praxia Plugin Interface**: unified plugin system for praxia (Rust, orchestration host), bathos (Python, experiment tracking), myxcel (Python, HPC infrastructure), jaxlint (Python, JAX linting)
- **manifest.toml**: plugin self-declaration file at `<plugin>/.praxia/manifest.toml`
- **Three-level registry**: global (`~/.praxia/plugins.toml`) → project (`.praxia/plugins.toml`) → local (`.praxia/plugins.local.toml`); resolution order local > project > global > manifest default
- **StandardWriter**: praxia owns ALL standard export writes (skills → `~/.claude/skills/<plugin>/<skill>/SKILL.md`, global snippets → `~/.claude/rules/<plugin>-<name>.md`, project snippets → `<project>/.claude/rules/<plugin>-<name>.md`, MCP → `~/.claude/settings.json`)
- **export_command**: plugin CLI post-step hook only — no file copying, just plugin-specific finishing logic
- **Scope model**: `global` | `project` | `off`; export destination follows scope
- **scope_detector**: `glob:`, `toml:file#key.path`, `env:VAR`; array = AND semantics; path resolution root = first ancestor with `.praxia/plugins.toml`, fallback git root, fallback CWD
- **Per-(plugin, scope_target) hash storage**: `hashes: BTreeMap<String, String>` keyed by `"_global"` or project root path; `exported_files: BTreeMap<String, Vec<String>>` same keying
- **Composite hash**: SHA-256 over manifest.toml bytes + all referenced asset file bytes (sorted by path)
- **ScopeDetector enum**: `Single(String)` | `Multiple(Vec<String>)` — Multiple requires ALL to match (AND)
- **`requires_praxia = "self"`**: valid only for plugin named "praxia"; skips version check; praxia bootstraps before other plugins
- **Uninstall safety**: reads `exported_files` union across all scope targets, deletes exactly those files (no glob)
- **session-init loop**: determines project_root, reads three registry levels, merges per plugin, runs scope detectors, checks hashes per (plugin, scope_target), calls StandardWriter only when stale
- **praxia plugin export**: on-demand CLI subcommand calling same session-init dirty-check loop

