8. Current Work:

Immediately before the summary request, the orchestrator was investigating Phase 8 (bth sync/run delegation to myxcel). The investigation revealed a fundamental mismatch between the spec's assumptions and actual bathos architecture.

Files read:
- `~/projects/bathos/src/bathos/sync.py`: `sync_catalog()` uses rsync for catalog parquet files at `.bth/catalog/runs/<slug>/`, with specific flags (`-az --partial --ignore-existing`, SSH options, 120s timeout). This is NOT project code sync.
- `~/projects/bathos/src/bathos/cli.py` (offset 55, limit 60): `bth sync` calls `sync_catalog`; `bth run` has no remote/sbatch dispatch
- `~/projects/bathos/tests/test_sync.py`: mocks assert `cmd[0] == "rsync"`, `-az` in cmd, SSH options present

The bathos CLAUDE.md (loaded via system-reminder) confirms: `bth sync` was shipped in v0.2 as "rsync cool-tier catalog to/from cluster remote" and never had project-code sync functionality.

Test mock signatures that would break if sync was changed to call myxcel:
